{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions).\n\nFrom enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, the unpaired held-out paragraph:\n\nUnpaired held-out (88): 10 are handled elsewhere (8 `tests/scripts/*_seam_clean_heldout.py` + `test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py` in S1, `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` deleted in S3); the remaining **78** are renamed to drop `_heldout` (unit 55, interfaces 18, scripts 4, integration 1). Three are cross-tier twins whose base lives in another directory and would collide on basename under pytest's prepend import mode (13 `__init__.py` files; no `--import-mode` in `pyproject.toml:8`): `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py` (base `tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py`) → `test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_baseline_normalization_heldout.py` (base in `tests/integration/…`) → `test_baseline_normalization_diffing.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_identity_264f_heldout.py` (base `tests/unit/test_identity_264f.py`) → `test_identity_264f_reconciler.py`. Do not merge across tiers.\n\n(\"S1\" and \"S3\" in that paragraph are the test-suite epic's stories E10a-S1 skaldic-paradoxal-huemul and E10a-S3 aware-obvious-sphinx.)\n\nRename mechanics:\n1. Enumerate the set at execution time, after S2, S3 and S4 have merged every pair: `git ls-files 'tests/**/test_*_heldout.py'` lists exactly the 78 files (the 10 handled elsewhere are already gone).\n2. For each file except the three cross-tier ones: `git mv tests/<dir>/test_<name>_heldout.py tests/<dir>/test_<name>.py` — the target basename does not exist anywhere under `tests/` (check with `git ls-files tests | xargs -n1 basename | sort | uniq -d` after the batch).\n3. The three cross-tier files take the `_store`, `_diffing` and `_reconciler` suffixes named above.\n4. `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py` → `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass.py`; it carries the tests E10a-S1 moved into it.\n5. No content change in any renamed module; the module docstrings keep their held-out \"what it proves\" paragraphs and every bug cite named in enumeration (6) (`test_sync_only_scalar_update_dispatch_heldout.py` af1b, `test_richtext_port_heldout.py` 1bb2-5da5 — merged in S2 —, `test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py` 0fad, `test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py` 7c26-4ac8-04a3-440e, `test_dc_pat_required_heldout.py` cd78, `test_dc_transition_by_status_heldout.py` 7f93, `test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py` 9263/deac, `test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py` deac, `test_identity_dc_inbound_heldout.py` 5f48, `test_identity_write_retention_heldout.py` 387d, `test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py` 21fc, `test_jira_key_local_id_heldout.py` 23ed, `test_retry_after_zero_guard_heldout.py` 3604-891f-e301-4aff, `test_identity_txn_signing_heldout.py` 0ba4, `test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py` beb1/ed5c, `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`).\n6. Record on this ticket one 78-row table: old path, new path, `pytest --collect-only -q` count before and after (equal per row).\n\nPaths under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` are stated at the current name (origin/main 083620b0); the reconciler epic (friended-brainsick-degus) rename carries them."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807578032455349,"uuid":"1183494f-cc83-4380-9d25-2d6d61abbf34"}